# Fix the producer

If something breaks, fix the **machinery that will fire next time** — prompts, skills, gates, importers, recipes, pickers — then regenerate. Do **not** hand-fix one bad artifact and call it done.

| Symptom | Fix here (then regen) |
|---------|------------------------|
| Formulaic / anonymous quiet flats | `.cursor/skills/bg-flat-sets` + `docs/bg-theme-sets.md` |
| Lesson ships without kit / hollow download | `BoardReadiness` / plan / prop kit assessment |
| Board teaches generate's first 6 while overflow had picturable words / hollow match | `VocabArt.adaptBoardVocabulary` + recipe pick in `edbActivities.plan` (same topic — never silent theme drift) |
| Bad prop keying or gate-blind art | import / prompt rules in `.cursor/skills/prop-cutouts` |
| Wrong activity shape (cards vs king stage) | recipes + `.cursor/skills/king-stage-edb` (no hero → `sortBins`, not dressUp lottery) |
| Weird lesson English / story≠questions / CEFR mismatch | prompts in `api/generate-lesson.js` + log row in `docs/content-wishlist.md` |
| StoryArt API down / quota | Caption + PropBank plates stay Ready path; StoryArt is opportunistic only |

**OK:** regenerating after the process fix; one-off data typos / a single manifest typo.

**Not OK:** Photoshop one PNG, tweak one fixture by hand, or ship a one-lesson special-case as the only fix while the producer still repeats the miss.
